## Remaining risks

- Fable's pre-existing unresolved risks stand: no cljd *test* runs (committed `test/dao/stream/ws_test.cljc` has no `:cljd` branch — outside this diff), pending sockets are not closed by `serving/stop!` so `:stopped` can be slow on Node with a lingering pending connection (the new bounded budget now bounds the wait rather than hanging), two shells (served vs local) under D4, and the unwired host seam.
- The shutdown path is proven by unit-level tests (`stop-tick`, `request-stop!`), not by an end-to-end host run; the signal handlers themselves are compile- and analyze-verified only.
- `verifyClient` is deprecated in `ws` 8 but present and used in its async form (the sync form hardcodes 401); a future `ws` major may require moving to an explicit `upgrade` handler.
- Step reordering (poll/observe before lines) shifts publication order within a tick: lifecycle notices now precede same-tick local results. Every existing assertion still holds.
